# Base dependencies from the gundi-integration-action-runner template.
#
# This file is INTENTIONALLY FORKED from the template on four pins:
# fastapi, gundi-core, gundi-client-v2 and httpx (see the notes on each).
# The fork cannot live in requirements.in: pip-compile intersects the
# constraints, so a `fastapi~=0.115` there against the template's `~=0.103`
# here is unresolvable. On the next template sync, do NOT take upstream's
# copy of this file wholesale; merge the other lines and keep these pins.
# Closing the fork means bumping these pins in the template first.
#
# imported directly by app/services/errors.py for exception classification
aiohttp
environs~=9.5.0
pydantic~=1.10.15
# forked: template pins ~=0.103.2; see the httpx note below
fastapi~=0.115.0
uvicorn~=0.23.2
# forked: template pins ~=1.11.1; 1.12 adds Event.provider_metadata, which the
# provider deep-link in deliver reads
gundi-core~=1.12.0
# forked: template pins ~=2.4.0; 3.x is needed for the generic-model rollout
# and scaffold write-back, and it requires httpx 0.28
gundi-client-v2~=3.3.0
# forked: httpx is imported directly by app/services/* so it must be declared
# here (template parity). The template pins ~=0.24.1 (tied to gundi-client-v2
# 2.4.0); gundi-client-v2 3.3.0 needs httpx 0.28. That is also why fastapi is
# ~=0.115 above rather than the template's ~=0.103: starlette 0.27's
# TestClient passes app= to httpx.Client, which httpx 0.28 removed, so the
# template's TestClient-based tests only collect on a newer starlette.
httpx~=0.28.1
stamina~=23.2.0
redis~=5.0.1
gcloud-aio-pubsub~=6.0.0
click~=8.1.7
pyjq~=2.6.0
python-json-logger~=2.0.7
marshmallow~=3.22.0
